native executables.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:21.770
Running your applications
as native executables,

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:24.830
rather than on the JVM
means smaller artifacts,

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:27.800
faster startup times, and lower
memory usage, all of which

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.590
allows you to get more work done
with resources that you already

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.430
have.

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:35.838
We'll get into the details of
why that is in just a moment.

00:01:35.838 --> 00:01:37.630
Spring Native makes
use of several concepts

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.470
and technologies to
make this happen,

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:42.152
including ahead-of-time
compilation and GraalVM.

00:01:42.152 --> 00:01:44.110
We'll talk a bit about
these before we actually

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:46.137
start using Spring Native.

00:01:46.137 --> 00:01:48.220
Currently, the project is
in an experimental phase

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:50.387
and is separate from the
main Spring and Spring Boot

00:01:50.387 --> 00:01:50.890
projects.

